     The password file is currently locked by another process; cchhppaassss will
     keep trying to lock the password file until it succeeds or the user hits
     the interrupt character (control-C by default).  If cchhppaassss is interrupted
     while trying to gain the lock, any changes made will be lost.

     If the process holding the lock was prematurely terminated, the lock file
     may be stale and cchhppaassss will wait forever trying to lock the password
     file.  To determine whether a live process is actually holding the lock,
     the admin may run the following:

           $ fstat /etc/ptmp

     If no process is listed, it is safe to remove the _/_e_t_c_/_p_t_m_p file to clear
     the error.

